    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 21.96,
      "end": 22.445,
      "duration": 0.485,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Good morning."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 22.445,
      "end": 24.39,
      "duration": 1.945,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Good morning."
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 24.39,
      "end": 25.0,
      "duration": 0.61,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: All right."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 25.0,
      "end": 28.65,
      "duration": 3.65,
      "text": "So today--"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 28.65,
      "end": 29.86,
      "duration": 1.21,
      "text": "I haven't seen you in a while."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 29.86,
      "end": 36.93,
      "duration": 7.07,
      "text": "Anyway, today, we're going to turn back to our picture,"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 36.93,
      "end": 39.27,
      "duration": 2.34,
      "text": "function gene protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 39.27,
      "end": 41.53,
      "duration": 2.26,
      "text": "We filled in genetics."
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 41.53,
      "end": 43.39,
      "duration": 1.86,
      "text": "We filled in biochemistry."
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 43.39,
      "end": 46.54,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "We've now got the connection between gene and protein"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 46.54,
      "end": 48.52,
      "duration": 1.98,
      "text": "through molecular biology."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 48.52,
      "end": 51.45,
      "duration": 2.93,
      "text": "We know gene encodes protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 51.45,
      "end": 53.73,
      "duration": 2.28,
      "text": "We know central dogma, DNA goes to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 53.73,
      "end": 55.56,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "RNA goes to the protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 55.56,
      "end": 57.1,
      "duration": 1.54,
      "text": "We know all that in theory."
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 57.1,
      "end": 63.82,
      "duration": 6.72,
      "text": "In fact, people knew this by the middle of the 1960s."
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 63.82,
      "end": 67.72,
      "duration": 3.9,
      "text": "People were so excited that they understood the idea of"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 67.72,
      "end": 72.13,
      "duration": 4.41,
      "text": "how genes give rise to proteins through transcription"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 72.13,
      "end": 77.89,
      "duration": 5.76,
      "text": "and translation, they read the genetic code, that they"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 77.89,
      "end": 79.62,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "declared victory."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 79.62,
      "end": 82.69,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "Some of them said, done with the secret of life."
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 82.69,
      "end": 84.56,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "Let's go on and do the brain."
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 84.56,
      "end": 86.99,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "That was actually the thinking of a lot of the great"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 86.99,
      "end": 89.38,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "molecular biologists in the late 1960s."
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 89.38,
      "end": 90.74,
      "duration": 1.36,
      "text": "Let's go do the brain."
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 90.74,
      "end": 92.78,
      "duration": 2.04,
      "text": "Why did they say such a thing?"
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 92.78,
      "end": 94.1,
      "duration": 1.32,
      "text": "Well, because they thought they were"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 94.1,
      "end": 96.17,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "done with the problem."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 96.17,
      "end": 99.44,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "They thought that once you knew in principle how a gene"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 99.44,
      "end": 101.98,
      "duration": 2.54,
      "text": "gave rise to a protein, you could do it."
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 101.98,
      "end": 108.22,
      "duration": 6.24,
      "text": "But in practice, nobody could read a single gene."
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 108.22,
      "end": 111.96,
      "duration": 3.74,
      "text": "Nobody could even identify a single gene."
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 111.96,
      "end": 113.98,
      "duration": 2.02,
      "text": "Maybe that's why they went on to say, let's go study the"
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 113.98,
      "end": 115.62,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "brain, because they actually weren't sure what they could"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 115.62,
      "end": 118.6,
      "duration": 2.98,
      "text": "do past that point."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 118.6,
      "end": 119.17,
      "duration": 0.57,
      "text": "All right."
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 119.17,
      "end": 121.43,
      "duration": 2.26,
      "text": "So wait a second, wait a second."
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 121.43,
      "end": 124.44,
      "duration": 3.01,
      "text": "I said nobody could even purify a single gene."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 124.44,
      "end": 128.661,
      "duration": 4.221,
      "text": "Didn't we talk about purifying the genetic material?"
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 128.661,
      "end": 130.91,
      "duration": 2.249,
      "text": "You're supposed to say yes at that point."
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 130.91,
      "end": 131.58,
      "duration": 0.67,
      "text": "Yes, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 131.58,
      "end": 132.63,
      "duration": 1.05,
      "text": "We talked about that."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 132.63,
      "end": 136.59,
      "duration": 3.96,
      "text": "Avery, McCarty, MacLeod-- we purified the genetic material."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 136.59,
      "end": 138.876,
      "duration": 2.286,
      "text": "We did it by using this assay of transforming."
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 141.48,
      "end": 144.22,
      "duration": 2.74,
      "text": "So what do I mean by we can't purify a single gene?"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 144.22,
      "end": 148.61,
      "duration": 4.39,
      "text": "What I mean is that we can purify the hereditary material"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 148.61,
      "end": 152.67,
      "duration": 4.06,
      "text": "away from everything else, but we get all of it together."
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 152.67,
      "end": 156.8,
      "duration": 4.13,
      "text": "We don't get individual genes separated from each other."
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 156.8,
      "end": 159.25,
      "duration": 2.45,
      "text": "We get the whole mixture of all the genes,"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 159.25,
      "end": 161.55,
      "duration": 2.3,
      "text": "all the genetic material."
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 161.55,
      "end": 164.91,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "As a biochemist, how are we going to ever separate the"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 164.91,
      "end": 166.24,
      "duration": 1.33,
      "text": "gene encoding--"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 166.24,
      "end": 169.52,
      "duration": 3.28,
      "text": "oh I don't know, ARG1, our favorite gene for arginine"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 169.52,
      "end": 170.58,
      "duration": 1.06,
      "text": "biosynthesis--"
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 170.58,
      "end": 174.67,
      "duration": 4.09,
      "text": "from the gene encoding ARG2, for example?"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 174.67,
      "end": 176.5,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "What kind of biochemistry can we do to"
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 176.5,
      "end": 177.88,
      "duration": 1.38,
      "text": "separate these two genes?"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 180.58,
      "end": 185.66,
      "duration": 5.08,
      "text": "Do they have different biochemical properties?"
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 185.66,
      "end": 187.35,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "What's so different about ARG1 and ARG2?"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 187.35,
      "end": 189.504,
      "duration": 2.154,
      "text": "What's their different biochemical properties?"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 189.504,
      "end": 191.79,
      "duration": 2.286,
      "text": "They're both DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 191.79,
      "end": 194.1,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "They have exactly the same building blocks, slightly"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 194.1,
      "end": 195.18,
      "duration": 1.08,
      "text": "different order."
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 195.18,
      "end": 197.35,
      "duration": 2.17,
      "text": "You think you have a purification procedure, I'm"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 197.35,
      "end": 199.8,
      "duration": 2.45,
      "text": "going to run it over some column and separate it by"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 199.8,
      "end": 204.04,
      "duration": 4.24,
      "text": "something that's going to separate ARG1 from ARG2?"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 204.04,
      "end": 204.57,
      "duration": 0.53,
      "text": "No."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 204.57,
      "end": 207.25,
      "duration": 2.68,
      "text": "From the point of view of a pure biochemist, they look"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 207.25,
      "end": 208.8,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "exactly the same."
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 208.8,
      "end": 211.92,
      "duration": 3.12,
      "text": "All the different genes have the same biochemical"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 211.92,
      "end": 213.44,
      "duration": 1.52,
      "text": "properties."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 213.44,
      "end": 218.32,
      "duration": 4.88,
      "text": "How in the world would we ever purify ARG1 from ARG2, or in"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 218.32,
      "end": 220.83,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "the human, the gene encoding hemoglobin from the gene"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 220.83,
      "end": 224.12,
      "duration": 3.29,
      "text": "encoding collagen from the gene encoding keratin from the"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 224.12,
      "end": 226.13,
      "duration": 2.01,
      "text": "gene encoding anything else?"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 226.13,
      "end": 226.67,
      "duration": 0.54,
      "text": "Think about it."
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 226.67,
      "end": 227.92,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "That's a tough problem."
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 230.34,
      "end": 234.97,
      "duration": 4.63,
      "text": "There is a brilliant solution that arose in the 1970s to how"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 234.97,
      "end": 238.33,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "we could purify the individual genes away from each other."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 238.33,
      "end": 241.18,
      "duration": 2.85,
      "text": "But it's like no other piece of biochemistry anybody had"
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 241.18,
      "end": 242.87,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "ever seen before."
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 242.87,
      "end": 246.08,
      "duration": 3.21,
      "text": "It has a totally different principle behind it."
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 246.08,
      "end": 249.86,
      "duration": 3.78,
      "text": "Because it isn't just fractionating things according"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 249.86,
      "end": 251.55,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "to their biochemical properties."
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 251.55,
      "end": 254.41,
      "duration": 2.86,
      "text": "It involves something else."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 254.41,
      "end": 256.1,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "And it's called cloning."
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 258.74,
      "end": 259.99,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "It is called cloning."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 262.4,
      "end": 264.095,
      "duration": 1.695,
      "text": "Molecular cloning."
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 264.095,
      "end": 265.52,
      "duration": 1.425,
      "text": "You see, the problem is this."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 265.52,
      "end": 268.35,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "The human genome--"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 268.35,
      "end": 270.76,
      "duration": 2.41,
      "text": "how big is the human genome?"
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 270.76,
      "end": 272.63,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "How many bases?"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 272.63,
      "end": 274.63,
      "duration": 2.0,
      "text": "Three billion bases, three times 10 to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 274.63,
      "end": 277.44,
      "duration": 2.81,
      "text": "ninth bases, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 277.44,
      "end": 280.15,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "How big is a typical human gene?"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 280.15,
      "end": 286.38,
      "duration": 6.23,
      "text": "A typical human gene might be 30,000 bases."
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 286.38,
      "end": 290.61,
      "duration": 4.23,
      "text": "How big is a typical mutation that we might want to find in"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 290.61,
      "end": 294.34,
      "duration": 3.73,
      "text": "a typical gene, like causing sickle cell anemia?"
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 294.34,
      "end": 297.29,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "One base."
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 297.29,
      "end": 300.58,
      "duration": 3.29,
      "text": "We've got to purify out genes that are one part in 10 to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 300.58,
      "end": 303.66,
      "duration": 3.08,
      "text": "fifth and mutations that are one part in 10 to"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 303.66,
      "end": 305.972,
      "duration": 2.312,
      "text": "the ninth or so."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 305.972,
      "end": 308.68,
      "duration": 2.708,
      "text": "And how are we going to do that?"
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 308.68,
      "end": 311.68,
      "duration": 3.0,
      "text": "Well, the trick is this."
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 311.68,
      "end": 314.01,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "I'll give you the quick overview, and then we'll spend"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 314.01,
      "end": 315.18,
      "duration": 1.17,
      "text": "today looking at it."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 315.18,
      "end": 319.15,
      "duration": 3.97,
      "text": "Step one is we cut up our DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 319.15,
      "end": 332.79,
      "duration": 13.64,
      "text": "We cut DNA at defined sites, and we then paste the DNA to"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 332.79,
      "end": 336.52,
      "duration": 3.73,
      "text": "distinct molecules called vectors."
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 336.52,
      "end": 340.64,
      "duration": 4.12,
      "text": "These vectors have a cool property, that when you take a"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 340.64,
      "end": 345.36,
      "duration": 4.72,
      "text": "vector and you insert in it a piece of DNA, that vector is"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 345.36,
      "end": 349.88,
      "duration": 4.52,
      "text": "able to grow in another organism."
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 349.88,
      "end": 352.84,
      "duration": 2.96,
      "text": "You then transform the DNA--"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 355.9,
      "end": 359.97,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "text": "that's transfer, we use the word transform the DNA--"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 359.97,
      "end": 363.55,
      "duration": 3.58,
      "text": "into something like E. coli, where you get your little"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 363.55,
      "end": 365.49,
      "duration": 1.94,
      "text": "vector in there."
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 365.49,
      "end": 370.11,
      "duration": 4.62,
      "text": "It grows within E. coli, and as E. coli divides, it makes"
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 370.11,
      "end": 371.68,
      "duration": 1.57,
      "text": "copies of itself."
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 371.68,
      "end": 383.75,
      "duration": 12.07,
      "text": "And then you select those bacteria that have received,"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 383.75,
      "end": 391.43,
      "duration": 7.68,
      "text": "that have been transformed, grow them up on a petri plate"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 391.43,
      "end": 395.46,
      "duration": 4.03,
      "text": "so that you have little colonies."
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 395.46,
      "end": 400.62,
      "duration": 5.16,
      "text": "And then you screen the colonies."
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 404.3,
      "end": 405.04,
      "duration": 0.74,
      "text": "Now, what do I mean?"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 405.04,
      "end": 405.96,
      "duration": 0.92,
      "text": "We cut the DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 405.96,
      "end": 407.02,
      "duration": 1.06,
      "text": "We paste the DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 407.02,
      "end": 408.75,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "We transform the DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 408.75,
      "end": 411.2,
      "duration": 2.45,
      "text": "We select the bacteria that have been successfully"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 411.2,
      "end": 412.09,
      "duration": 0.89,
      "text": "transformed."
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 412.09,
      "end": 414.61,
      "duration": 2.52,
      "text": "And we screen the resulting colonies to find what we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 414.61,
      "end": 415.51,
      "duration": 0.9,
      "text": "looking for."
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 415.51,
      "end": 416.42,
      "duration": 0.91,
      "text": "Now, notice--"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 416.42,
      "end": 418.99,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "that amazing trick here is when we cut up the DNA into"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 418.99,
      "end": 421.91,
      "duration": 2.92,
      "text": "single molecules, lots and lots of single molecules, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 421.91,
      "end": 426.46,
      "duration": 4.55,
      "text": "we paste them into vectors, and we transform them into"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 426.46,
      "end": 431.88,
      "duration": 5.42,
      "text": "bacteria, each one of those bacteria gets exactly one"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 431.88,
      "end": 434.45,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "molecule, give or take."
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 434.45,
      "end": 437.93,
      "duration": 3.48,
      "text": "It gets one piece of human DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 437.93,
      "end": 439.81,
      "duration": 1.88,
      "text": "We then spread them out on a plate and they grow up, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 439.81,
      "end": 442.84,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "each one grows up copies for us of"
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 442.84,
      "end": 445.02,
      "duration": 2.18,
      "text": "individual pieces of DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 445.02,
      "end": 446.42,
      "duration": 1.4,
      "text": "That is so cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 446.42,
      "end": 448.12,
      "duration": 1.7,
      "text": "Because we've just accomplished biochemical"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 448.12,
      "end": 449.79,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "purification."
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 449.79,
      "end": 451.85,
      "duration": 2.06,
      "text": "It's not based on any different properties of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 451.85,
      "end": 453.19,
      "duration": 1.34,
      "text": "individual molecules."
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 453.19,
      "end": 456.06,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "It's based on the fact that we dilute them, in effect."
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 456.06,
      "end": 457.8,
      "duration": 1.74,
      "text": "They're diluted, and one molecule"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 457.8,
      "end": 459.62,
      "duration": 1.82,
      "text": "ends up in each bacteria."
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 459.62,
      "end": 461.44,
      "duration": 1.82,
      "text": "So they're purified in that sense."
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 461.44,
      "end": 463.98,
      "duration": 2.54,
      "text": "And then when that bacteria grows up, everything it grows"
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 463.98,
      "end": 467.62,
      "duration": 3.64,
      "text": "up is a pure copy, a copy of that single piece of DNA that"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 467.62,
      "end": 469.02,
      "duration": 1.4,
      "text": "went into it."
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 469.02,
      "end": 473.03,
      "duration": 4.01,
      "text": "That's a different kind of purification."
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 473.03,
      "end": 474.84,
      "duration": 1.81,
      "text": "When I'm done-- and we'll go through this whole process."
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 474.84,
      "end": 476.365,
      "duration": 1.525,
      "text": "That's the point of today's lecture, is to go through the"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 476.365,
      "end": 476.88,
      "duration": 0.515,
      "text": "whole process."
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 476.88,
      "end": 478.77,
      "duration": 1.89,
      "text": "When I'm done, I have bacteria spread out."
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 478.77,
      "end": 481.26,
      "duration": 2.49,
      "text": "And right over there, one of these guys has ARG1, and one"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 481.26,
      "end": 484.74,
      "duration": 3.48,
      "text": "of these guys has ARG2, and one of these guys has ARG10."
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 484.74,
      "end": 486.8,
      "duration": 2.06,
      "text": "Now, admittedly, I don't know which one has which, but I've"
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 486.8,
      "end": 489.74,
      "duration": 2.94,
      "text": "accomplished the purification."
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 489.74,
      "end": 492.07,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "I'll then have to figure out how to screen and find out"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 492.07,
      "end": 495.3,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "which one is which, but I have separated the molecules away"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 495.3,
      "end": 498.95,
      "duration": 3.65,
      "text": "from each other by this process of cloning, diluting"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 498.95,
      "end": 500.54,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "them in a way--"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 500.54,
      "end": 502.53,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "one molecule per bacteria--"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 502.53,
      "end": 504.961,
      "duration": 2.431,
      "text": "and growing them back up."
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 504.961,
      "end": 506.3,
      "duration": 1.339,
      "text": "I could do this for anything."
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 506.3,
      "end": 509.69,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "I could dilute proteins down into test tubes that had one"
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 509.69,
      "end": 512.919,
      "duration": 3.229,
      "text": "protein molecule per test tube, and I could say I've"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 512.919,
      "end": 515.1,
      "duration": 2.181,
      "text": "accomplished purification."
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 515.1,
      "end": 517.11,
      "duration": 2.01,
      "text": "The problem with it is I have no way to replicate those"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 517.11,
      "end": 519.32,
      "duration": 2.21,
      "text": "proteins to get a meaningful amount of it."
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 519.32,
      "end": 522.48,
      "duration": 3.16,
      "text": "But when it's DNA, and I've put it back into a bacteria, I"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 522.48,
      "end": 524.02,
      "duration": 1.54,
      "text": "have a way to grow it back up."
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 524.02,
      "end": 525.73,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "And that's why this trick works--"
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 525.73,
      "end": 528.94,
      "duration": 3.21,
      "text": "is because DNA is a molecule that can replicate."
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 528.94,
      "end": 531.55,
      "duration": 2.61,
      "text": "No other molecule has that cool property."
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 531.55,
      "end": 533.5,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "And so you can pull this off for DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 533.5,
      "end": 534.05,
      "duration": 0.55,
      "text": "All right."
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 534.05,
      "end": 536.16,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "Now we have to dive in to understand how this could"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 536.16,
      "end": 537.41,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "possibly work."
    }
  ],
